  "question": "Background / Context:\n\nThe project involves processing transactional data from a Czech debit card company that specializes in facilitating payments at petrol pumps. The data includes customer information, gas station details, products sold, and transaction specifics.\n\nObjectives:\n\nThe primary objective is to develop a system that accurately tracks and manages transactions for payments made using debit cards at petrol stations. The system should facilitate the monitoring of customer transactions, manage gas station operations, and provide detailed reporting on product sales.\n\nStakeholders & Users:\n\n1. Customers: Individuals using debit cards for purchasing fuel and other products at petrol stations.\n2. Gas Station Operators: Manage the operations and inventory of gas stations.\n3. Debit Card Company: Requires detailed transaction records for compliance, reporting, and analysis.\n4. Data Analysts: Use the information for generating insights and reporting.\n\nFunctional Descriptions:\n\n1. Customer Management: \n   - Track customer segments and currency preferences.\n\n2. Transaction Processing:\n   - Record transaction details including date, time, customer ID, card ID, gas station ID, product ID, amount, and price.\n   - Support cascading updates and deletions to maintain data integrity.\n\n3. Gas Station Management:\n   - Store and manage information about gas stations, including chain affiliations and geographic locations.\n\n4. Product Management:\n   - Maintain a catalog of products available at petrol stations.\n\n5. Transaction Recording:\n   - Support both standard and detailed transaction records with unique transaction IDs for high-volume records.\n\n6. Consumption Tracking:\n   - Capture monthly consumption data for each customer based on transactions.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions:\n\n1. Scalability: \n   - The system should efficiently handle a large volume of transactional data.\n\n2. Data Integrity:\n   - Ensure data consistency through foreign key constraints and cascading updates/deletes.\n\n3. Performance:\n   - Optimize query performance for reporting and transaction retrieval operations.\n\n4. Security:\n   - Protect sensitive customer and transaction data in compliance with relevant financial regulations.\n\n5. Usability:\n   - Provide intuitive access and navigation for stakeholders, ensuring efficiency in data handling and reporting.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0096\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `segment` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `currency` char(3) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `gas_station_chain` (\n  `chain_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `chain_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`chain_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `gas_station` (\n  `gas_station_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `chain_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `station_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `region` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `latitude` decimal(10,6) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `longitude` decimal(10,6) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`gas_station_id`),\n  KEY `chain_id` (`chain_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `gas_station_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`chain_id`) REFERENCES `gas_station_chain` (`chain_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `product_category` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `card` (\n  `card_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `card_number_hash` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `issue_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `expiry_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`card_id`),\n  KEY `customer_id` (`customer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `card_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `transaction_record` (\n  `transaction_id` bigint(20) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_time` time NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `card_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `gas_station_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(12,2) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(12,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`transaction_id`),\n  KEY `customer_id` (`customer_id`),\n  KEY `card_id` (`card_id`),\n  KEY `gas_station_id` (`gas_station_id`),\n  KEY `product_id` (`product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`card_id`) REFERENCES `card` (`card_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_record_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`gas_station_id`) REFERENCES `gas_station` (`gas_station_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_record_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `monthly_consumption` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `consumption_year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `consumption_month` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_amount` decimal(14,2) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_count` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`,`consumption_year`,`consumption_month`),\n  CONSTRAINT `monthly_consumption_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
